model {
  extend basalt {
    stageCloudflare = module "Test stage account API" {
      #basalt
      description "The one deployment provider caller for isolated test stages, shared by the scale test and the emulated upstream and open to any further stage tool without a copy. A caller names its stage prefix, and optionally a predicate that narrows it, and gets back operations, never paths or URLs: the stage's container applications, runtime adapters and their namespaces (a namespace is owned through the runtime adapter that defines it), database connection configs and client certificates listed account-wide at once; a read, patch, rollout or delete of a row that listing returned, or a runtime adapter's settings by its name; the account's Worker subdomain; the image references the account's container applications run; and the stage's registry repositories with their tags, deleted index first. Every operation is one structured request to a single choke point, the only code that holds the network client: a declared kind, a declared operation of that kind, a listed row or adapter name, and a body. It builds each URL from a fixed template per kind and operation and refuses before sending unless every name in it is inside the stage's registered prefix and no name the release stack's records use, and every id or registry reference is one this stage's own listing recorded for that name, unchanged since and free of separators, dots, escapes, query, fragment and whitespace. Account-wide reads take nothing from the caller, and their rows are filtered by ownership before they are returned. Construction refuses a prefix that holds a release stage word, starts like a release stack name or is not registered, and a predicate that accepts a release stack name. Tests check that exactly one call of the network client exists in the module, enumerate every exported operation and every declared kind and operation so an uncovered one fails, and send each hostile input (dot segments, escaped separators, absolute paths and URLs, query and fragment characters, rows changed after listing or of another kind, look-alike prefixes and production names) against a recorded-shapes account whose every received URL is judged against the stage's own resources. Every account read fails closed: a refused call, a false success envelope or a listing without its array throws, so a wrong template or a missing permission never reads as an empty account. Only a read of one resource answers absent, on 404. Refusals carry the operation, status, error codes and known field names, never remote messages. It holds no credential of its own."
      metadata {
        code "scripts/stage-cloudflare"
      }
    }
  }
  basalt.stageCloudflare -[sync]-> deploymentProvider "list, read, patch, roll out and delete only a stage's own resources, and mint short-lived registry credentials, failing closed on any refusal"
  basalt.stageCloudflare -[sync]-> containerRegistry "list a stage's own repositories and tags and delete their manifests"
  basalt.scaleTest -[sync]-> basalt.stageCloudflare "find, change and delete only the scale stage's resources"
  basalt.emulatedUpstream -[sync]-> basalt.stageCloudflare "find and delete only the emulated stage's resources and registry images"
}
